LocalRouter's change to plotarmordev/drama-tensorfold's recipe/pilot.py (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026
plotarmordev), at 1a53b8aea738a99d3630f949b6b2a1f9389f0795. It adds --external-admission: when an outer scheduler
(LocalRouter) admits the load from its own memory budget, the launcher skips its MemAvailable admission (88 GiB) and
its 34 GiB abort, and gives the engine its least memory reserve (TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB=2 instead of 34), so
the engine does not refuse a load the scheduler admitted. Its cgroup cap (54 GiB), the server's allocator cap
(TENSORFOLD_CUDA_MEMORY_LIMIT_GB=54) and its lock are unchanged. This patch is licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
fetch.sh applies it with `git apply` to a copy at ROOT/launcher/pilot.py.

